Track 2: Chalk-Squares Chew the Flood
- Story & Context: Written in a floating tarp-shanty wedged between two drowned bridge pylons, this bittersweet confessional recounts a childhood hopscotch game where stepping on the wet salt-bleached tiles meant your memories were officially surrendered to the bayou. Ha-neul spent sixteen hours tuning her five-string banjo to open-G using seawater drops to calibrate the tension of the dried catgut strings, weeping openly as the tropical squall rattled the tin roof. "Don't apologize until your toes turn to salt," she murmurs over a wheezing, rotating melodica riff that mimics the siren song of submerged dredging barges.
