Track 3: Old Man Baek’s Rust-Lantern Arcade
- Story & Context: The EP concludes with the urban myth of Old Man Baek, a legendary bootlegger who ran an arcade of water-damaged pachinko machines inside the top floor observation deck of the Sunken Spire. During the great storm of '89, Baek allegedly drowned holding his favorite melodica, but night divers still swear they can hear a swinging ragtime banjo melody and reedy breath-notes vibrating up through the rusted elevator cables. "The roof gave up, but the morning never learned how to sink," goes the soaring final chorus, punctuated by ringing steel-pan triplets, soaring slide guitar, and the triumphant, communal chorus of a city that refuses to go under.
